  "about": "Article XII's step 7 — the routes a call takes once it has survived the six steps before it. Four of the five are the warden answering, and all four are pinned exactly. The fifth, a being invoked with a method, is reached by the same routing but its answer is not pinned anywhere and will not be: what a being answers belongs to its blueprint, and a scenario naming a value there would be asserting a being this harness invented. The corpus cannot express any of this — which route a call takes is a fact about a door with records, and the routes differ in what they answer rather than in what arrives.",
