      "name": "neither a being nor a method is a describe of what that voice reaches",
      "law": "The judgment",
      "obligations": ["XII-7", "XII-9", "XII-3"],
      "derivation": "An ask carrying no being and no method. Article XII's route list: \"Neither — the warden describes the estate, which means what that voice may reach, read off the inbound record.\" And there is no ambiguity about what an ask with nothing in it means: \"There is no empty ask, because there is a default one: describe. And the describe is the warden's answer, never the being's.\" So the answer is the estate this voice reaches — the Counter being it holds a standing on, and the public being everyone reaches — in digest order. **The voice is also a far warden this door holds a relation with**, which is what makes this an XII-3 case: step 4 places the voice \"in the two records and in that order\", inbound before outbound, so it is a holder and this is an ask. A door that looked at its outbound record first would find the same key there and call this news, which is answered with nothing at all.",
