      "name": "a method with no being is the warden's own being, and answers the same",
      "law": "The judgment",
      "obligations": ["XII-7", "XII-8"],
      "derivation": "The same describe, addressed the other way: a method and no being. Article XII: \"Method, no being — the warden's own being answers.\" And the two addresses are one being: \"The warden's own being answers to two addresses, and that is meant. Naming it is the ordinary form; omitting it is the shortcut for a stranger who holds a card and has described nothing yet. Nothing is identified by how a call was addressed, so nothing here can diverge.\" So this answer carries byte-for-byte the data the exchange above carries — the same estate value, built once — and differs only in the seq, which names the ask it answers. A door that routed the two addresses to two places would miss this pin, which is how XII-8 is asserted without comparing two answers to each other.",
